Source file: unifont-17.0.05.otf, release 17.0.05.

The file is kept unmodified so that the Unicode coverage and font
metadata remain intact. It is a CFF flavoured OpenType font with 58910
code points, covering the Basic Multilingual Plane along with parts of
the supplementary planes, and 64 units per em because the outlines are
derived from a 16 pixel bitmap grid. The Unicode viewer (/bin/unicode)
uses it as its glyph source; it renders at multiples of 16 pixels so
that the bitmap grid lands on whole pixels.

Colour emoji are not part of Unifont and are not covered here.
